From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 08:54:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bonito/sargo: drop the includes lineage-24.0 no longer has

This device tree is 22.2 and the platform is 24.0, so three includes point at files that no longer
exist and product config stops before lunch:

- hardware/google/pixel/PixelLogger -- gone from the same repo. A logging tool, not a HAL.
- device/google/gs-common/thermal/thermal_hal -- gs-common's thermal/ is empty at the pinned branch.

The PixelLogger include is commented rather than deleted, with the reason, because it is a thing to
restore rather than a thing that was wrong. The thermal include is deleted outright; what it
packaged is put back by the thermal HAL patch later in this series. The vibrator include stays:
hardware/google/pixel 0001 restores the drv2624 HAL it needs. The first question is whether a 22.2 device tree configures
and compiles against Android 17 at all, and none of these affects that.

The one other missing include, vendor/google_devices/bonito/proprietary/BoardConfigVendor.mk, is a
`-include` and absent on 22.2 as well -- it has never been there and does not fail.
---
 device.mk | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/device.mk b/device.mk
index 4d697a25..b7a4cb44 100644
--- a/device.mk
+++ b/device.mk
@@ -721,7 +721,6 @@ PRODUCT_VENDOR_PROPERTIES += ro.soc.model=SDM670
 
 include hardware/google/pixel/vibrator/drv2624/device.mk
 include hardware/google/pixel/mm/device_legacy.mk
-include device/google/gs-common/thermal/thermal_hal/device.mk
 
 # Citadel
 include hardware/google/pixel/citadel/citadel.mk
@@ -730,4 +729,6 @@ include hardware/google/pixel/citadel/citadel.mk
 -include hardware/google/pixel/power-libperfmgr/aidl/device.mk
 
 # Pixel Logger
-include hardware/google/pixel/PixelLogger/PixelLogger.mk
+# lineage-24.0: PixelLogger is gone from hardware/google/pixel too. A logging tool, not a HAL --
+# nothing depends on it to boot.
+#include hardware/google/pixel/PixelLogger/PixelLogger.mk
